  "text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n2026 Primary Election (June 2, 2026) - Elections - Poweshiek County, Iowa\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n Poweshiek County, Iowa\n Election Central\n \n \n\n \n\n Contact Us\n \n \n\n \n \nHome\n \nVote \n \n \nRegister to Vote\n \nAbsentee Voting\n \nMaps\n \nMilitary/Overseas Voting\n \nPrecincts\n \nVoter ID\n \n \n \nElections \n \n \nUpcoming Elections\n \nPast Elections\n \nSample Ballots\n \nPrecinct Election Officials\n \nTypes of Elections\n \n \n \nElected Officials \n \n \nFederal\n \nState\n \nCounty\n \nCity\n \nRural Improvement Zone\n \nSchool Board\n \nTownship\n \n \n \nCandidates\n \nNews\n \nFAQ\n \n \n \n\n \n\n\n\n\n Poweshiek County\nElections\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nElections 2026 Primary Election\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nElections by Year\n\n \n2026 \n2025 \n2024 \n2023 \n2022 \n2021 \n2020 \n2019 \n2018 \n2017 \n2016 \nView All\n\n\nElections\n\n \nUpcoming Elections\n \nPast Elections\n \nSample Ballots\n \nPrecinct Election Officials\n \nTypes of Elections\n\n \n \n\n \n2026 Primary Election\n\n \nJune 2, 2026\n Primary Election \n \n\n The Primary Election is an election to determine which candidates will qualify for the General Election for a given party. In Iowa you must be a member of the political party of which you wish to vote for in order to participate. This is known as a \"closed primary.\" The primary election is held on the 1st Tuesday following the 1st Monday in June of each even-numbered year. \n\n \n \n \n \n\n \nElection Results\n \n\n Download Official Results\n \n \n\n \n \n\n \n \n\n \n\n Write-In Report · Official\n \n \n\n \n \n\n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n \n \n \nArchived Election Details\n \nSCROLL DOWN FOR IMPORTANT DATES: \n \n\nPrimaries will be held for the Democrat and Republican Parties on June 2, 2026. Primaries are closed in the State of Iowa, which means a voter will need to declare a party (Democrat or Republican) to participate in the primary. Primary winners will advance to the November 3, 2026, General Election. Polling places will be open on Election Day from 7 a.m. - 8 p.m. \n \n\nCandidate Information: \n \n\nThe Poweshiek County Auditor's Office has packets available for those wanting to appear on the 2026 Primary Election ballot for County Attorney, County Recorder, County Treasurer, or County Supervisor. \n \n\nCandidates will complete an affidavit of candidacy, along with a nomination petition with at least 75 signatures from eligible voters in Poweshiek County. \n \n\nCandidate filing will begin March 2, 2026, and end at 5:00 p.m. on March 20, 2026. \n \n\nVoter Registration Information: \n \n\nPre-registered voters are now required to provide an approved form of identification at the polling place before receiving and casting a regular ballot. Voters who are not pre-registered (such as voters registering on Election Day, and voters changing precincts), must also provide proof of residence.  The following documents can be used as proof of residency if they contain your name and current address, and are current within 45 days:  Residential lease, utility bill, bank statement, paycheck, government check or other government document, or a property tax statement (current within 45 days of final payment date).  Voters who are unable to provide an approved form of identification (or prove residence if required) may have their identities attested to by another registered voter in the precinct or have the right to cast a provisional ballot.  Attesters must also provide an approved form of identification.  For additional information about providing proof of identity and/or residency, you may visit the Secretary of State’s website at: https://sos.iowa.gov/voterid, or contact the Poweshiek County Auditor’s Office at 641-623-5543.  \n \n\nPre-Election Day voter registration for this election will close Monday, May 18, 2026, at 5:00 p.m.  It is highly recommended that those persons wishing to vote in this election should pre-register on or before May 18, 2026.  Eligible persons have the right to register to vote and cast a ballot on Election Day if they can provide proof of both their identity and residency at the polls.  Please bring a valid and current photo ID that has an expiration date.  If the address on your ID is not current, you will also need to provide proof of residency.  \n \n\nAbsentee Voting: \n \n\nVoters may start sending in absentee ballot request forms beginning Tuesday, March 24, 2026. Absentee ballots requests may be mailed or delivered to the Poweshiek County Auditor, 302 E. Main St., PO Box 57, Montezuma, IA 50171 \n \n\nTo request an absentee ballot, you will need to complete an absentee ballot request form. Make sure you fill out the form completely, designate your party affiliation, sign and date the form, and mail it to the Poweshiek County Auditor. Absentee request forms may be requested from the Poweshiek County Auditor's Office, 641-623-5443, on our election website, or on the SOS website https://sos.iowa.gov.   \n \n\nAbsentee voting will begin on Wednesday, May 13, 2026. The last day to request an absentee ballot to be mailed to your home is Monday, May 18, 2026, at 5:00 p.m. \n \n\nVoted absentee ballots must be returned to the Poweshiek County Auditor's Office by the close of polls on Election Day (8:00 p.m.) \n \n\nIn-person absentee voting is available at the Poweshiek County Auditor's Office during regular business hours (8:00 a.m. - 4:00 p.m.) beginning Wednesday, May 13, 2026, until Monday, June 1, 2026.  \n \n\nAuditor's Office will be open Saturday, May 30, 2026, from 7:30 a.m. to 3:30 p.m. for absentee voting. \n \n\nSatellite voting petition deadline is Thursday, April 16, 2026. \n \n\nSATELLITE VOTING – MAY 13, 2026, 9:00 A.M. TO 3:00 P.M. AT GRINNELL COLLEGE, JRC, ROOM 101 \n \n\n  \n \n \n\n \nSample Ballots (PDF)\n \n\n Democratic – All Precincts\n \n \n\n Republican – All Precincts\n \n \n\n \nBack: Past Elections\n \n \n\n\n\n\nThis webpage was printed on October 17, 2026. For the most current election-related information, visit the Poweshiek County, Iowa, Elections website at https://poweshiekcounty.iowa.gov.\n\n\n \n\n Poweshiek County Courthouse\n\n 302 East Main\n \nP.O. Box 57\n \nMontezuma, IA 50171\n\n Contact Us\n\n Accessibility\n\n Poweshiek County Website\n \n \nOffice Hours\n\n 8:00 a.m. to 4:00 p.m.\n \nMonday through Friday \n \nContact Information\n\n (641) 623-5443 \n \n\n \n\n Contact Us\n \n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n \npowered by \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"
